<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M3, AC3.6 / T18: FLIPPING LINEAR AND CLOSURE WHILE THE TRANSPORT
  RUNS COSTS AT MOST THE HOUSE BOUND OF 1024 FRAMES, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.

  The flip is a real re-plumbing, not a mode bit. Entering a Closure the RT
  stops adding the frozen root page, the pump's master node gains the lane's
  inserts and gain, the frozen lane RE-ROOTS below the master chain (AC3.1) and
  the master's processors become live-owned. Leaving one undoes all four, in the
  opposite order. Every one of those is a chance to drop audio.

  THE MASTER INSERT IS AT UNITY, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE DESIGN OF THIS CASE.
  masterChainStateOf counts INSERTS, so a unity-gain plugin makes the shape
  non-linear exactly as a 2.0x one does, but it changes no level. So the
  output must be CONTINUOUS AND UNCHANGED across both flips, and a gap, a step
  or a level move is then the defect with nothing to disentangle it from. The
  2.0x master the other cases use would put a real 6 dB step at each flip and
  force every bound to be loose enough to admit it.

  THE UNARMED TRACK IS HELD AT -60 dB so the measurement is the RING, whose
  level is the same in both modes: under LINEAR the ring bypasses the master
  (unity, so no change) and under CLOSURE it goes through it (unity, so no
  change).

  THE INPUT IS test_autosaw.wav, NOT the test_sawtooth.wav the other master
  cases take, and the difference is load-bearing. test_sawtooth.wav RAMPS in
  amplitude over its 4 s and then loops, so the RMS of a window depends on WHERE
  that window sits and no fixed band is a closed form at an arbitrary position.
  A first draft of this case measured three 16000-frame windows against one
  band and failed two of them for exactly that reason, with nothing wrong in the
  engine. test_autosaw.wav is CONSTANT amplitude (RMS 0.230956, a 480 Hz
  sawtooth whose period is exactly 100 frames), so 0.25 gain puts every window
  at 0.230956 x 0.25 = 0.057739 wherever it is placed.

  TWO INDEPENDENT MEASUREMENTS, because a flip can fail two ways:

    assert-audio-continuity   no run of silence longer than 1024 frames
                              anywhere across BOTH flips
    assert-audio-energy       the level is the same before, during and after

  Continuity alone would pass a flip that halved the level without dropping a
  sample; energy alone would pass one that dropped 900 frames and recovered.

  1024 IS THE HOUSE BOUND AND IT IS NOT ARBITRARY (proposal 21 L2): the RT sums
  a ring entry only when its stamp matches the frame being delivered, so a miss
  is one DEVICE BLOCK wide by construction. Anything tighter asserts something
  the design does not offer, which is the mistake
  live_instrument_disarm_playback made before its 512 moved to the frozen side.

  maxStep is deliberately NOT checked. It would need the fixture's own
  peak-to-peak reset as its unit, and this case already makes the stronger
  statement (the level is the SAME on both sides of both flips) through a
  closed form rather than through a bound on a difference.

  TIMING. The flips land at roughly 2.2 s and 3.4 s of CAPTURED audio, and the
  window is [96000, 200000) = 2.0 to 4.17 s, which contains both with margin at
  each end. Capture frame 0 is the DEVICE start, which is after the monitor
  priming lag, so the window is past it by construction.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="monitor_master_flip_midplay">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- Track 0: armed and monitored, on the paced file input carrying
         test_sawtooth.wav (RMS 0.328284), through a 0.25 gain = 0.082071. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-input trackPath="0" input="audio:file:3"/>
    <set-monitor-mode trackPath="0" mode="on"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="0.25"/>

    <!-- Track 1: NEVER armed, held at -60 dB, so what is measured is the ring.
         Placed twice for 8 s. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="192000"/>
    <set-track-volume trackPath="1" volume="-60"/>

    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="1"/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <wait-ms ms="2200"/>

    <!-- FLIP 1: LINEAR to CLOSURE, at unity. -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="1.0"/>
    <wait-ms ms="1200"/>

    <!-- BISECT: entering the closure on its own must already be clean, so a
         failure at the end of the case is attributable to the LEAVING flip. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>

    <!-- FLIP 2: CLOSURE back to LINEAR. -->
    <remove-plugin trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0"/>
    <wait-ms ms="1000"/>

    <toggle-playback play="0"/>
    <dump-playback-capture filename="master_flip_midplay.wav" minFrames="200000"/>

    <!-- AC3.6: neither flip dropped more than one device block. -->
    <assert-audio-continuity filename="master_flip_midplay.wav"
                             startFrame="96000" frameCount="104000" channel="0"
                             maxGapFrames="1024" maxStep="-1"
                             silenceLevel="0.002"/>

    <!-- ...and neither flip moved the level. Before flip 1, between the two,
         and after flip 2. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="master_flip_midplay.wav"
                         startFrame="96000" frameCount="16000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.0560" maxRms="0.0595"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="master_flip_midplay.wav"
                         startFrame="132000" frameCount="16000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.0560" maxRms="0.0595"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="master_flip_midplay.wav"
                         startFrame="180000" frameCount="16000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.0560" maxRms="0.0595"/>

    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="0"/>

    <!-- AC3.4 across BOTH flips: entering re-roots before taking ownership and
         leaving releases before re-rooting back, so no freeze worker ever meets
         a live-owned master processor. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
